  "note": "Self-written release notes and changelogs (変更履歴・リリースノート / changelog, release notes) for made-up software: a desktop app's changelog with one heading per release, newest first, and a mobile app's release notes for one version with a table of earlier releases and a support section, each in a clean version and a planted one that differs only on the lines below. They run as technical/readme, the genre a changelog file is guessed as. Each mistake names its kind, the line it is on, the text the clean line has there (clean) and the planted line has instead (planted), and the rule expected to report it on that line; an end of support written as its own labelled line names the release date line as pairedLine. A version out of order is planted so that only one version breaks the order: with four releases, a version that could be swapped with its neighbour leaves two longest runs and the rule rightly says nothing. The end of support written as a labelled line is named for due-before-issue, whose date pairs do not yet list a release date and an end of support. A rule that does not exist yet is named as the rule that should: version-notation-variant (one version written in two forms in one document, 2.4.0 and v2.4.0, or 3.0.0 and 3.0). yarn planted releasenotes scores them; expected.json is the committed score.",
